{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "two-color grid where one color forms a one-pixel L on two adjacent outer edges and the other color fills the opposite rectangle",
  "transform": "use the L corner as orientation; recolor the outer L to the fill color, draw the next inner L in the original L color, keep the fill color only on the main diagonal of the remaining inner rectangle, and recolor all other pixels to gray"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 5-10 rows x 6-10 cols, minimum 3 in each dimension
  input_structure: |
    Exactly two colors (neither is 8/azure). One color forms a 1-cell-thick
    L-shape on two adjacent outer edges meeting at one corner. The other color
    fills the remaining (h-1)x(w-1) rectangle.
  L_corner: any of TL, TR, BL, BR (all four orientations appear across examples)
  colors: any two distinct colors from 0-9 excluding 8; one is border_color (the L), other is fill_color
  output_structure: |
    Same grid size. Three colors: border_color, fill_color, 8.
    Canonicalize L to top-left corner, then:
      - Row 0, cols 1..w-1 = fill_color (outer L top arm replaced)
      - Col 0, rows 1..h-1 = fill_color (outer L left arm replaced)
      - Row 1, cols 2..w-1 = border_color (inner L top arm)
      - Col 1, rows 2..h-1 = border_color (inner L left arm)
      - Diagonal from (2,2) to (2+k,2+k) for k in 0..min(h-3,w-3) = fill_color
      - All other cells = 8
    Then flip back to original orientation.
  diagonal_length: min(h-2, w-2), range 3-8

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is trivial to build)
  steps:
    - Pick h in [5,10], w in [5,10], ensuring h>=3 and w>=3
    - Pick two distinct colors from 0-9 excluding 8 for border_color and fill_color
    - Pick a corner from {TL, TR, BL, BR}
    - Build grid filled with fill_color
    - Paint the L (full row + full column at chosen corner edges) with border_color
